{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1089270-advice-on-a-gm-cult","id":1089270,"title":"Advice on a GM cult.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T11:23:45-07:00","id":1089270,"title":"Advice on a GM cult.","content":"I came up with a antagonist to use in a Demon game and i want advice on it. It is basically a self-help company called Silverthorn Counseling. It was founded by a man named Arthur Osborn, a former hippie and best selling self-help author. He founded the company after returning from Asia and introducing a new system of meditation he discovered in a obscure monastery in Thailand. He calls it a way to get in tune with the inner mechanisms of the cosmos. In reality, it is a bloodthirsty cult that worships the God Machine. The meditation the monastery taught Arthur was a way to contact a extension of the God Machine and eventually with repeated sessions, make you a stigmatic. The cult's corporate hq is in Beverly Hills, California and has over 5,000 employees.<br /> <br /> I want help on fleshing out the cult and how to make them a threat to demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:53:39-07:00","id":1089468,"title":"","content":"You could always have them become sleepers before they become stigmatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T20:38:59-07:00","id":1089558,"title":"","content":"How much G-M backing does Silverthorn Counseling have? The Knights of St. Adrian set a precedent for an angel giving mortals, apparently on a whim, a set of endowments that let them combat demons. Perhaps different levels of initiation has a similar effect: letting adherents use effects like Voice of the Machine or City Walking. Does Arthur Osborn have an angelic minder or puppet master (An exile, perhaps)? Maybe there's a Concealment Infrastructure that prevents Demons from purchasing membership in the cult and incorporating it into an existing cover or patch job (DTD does allude that the ability of demons to make pacts is the artifact of an existing G-M system.) <br /> <br /> What mundane resources does Silverthorn Counseling have? 5,000 employees and a corporate HQ implies fluid capital, plus celebrity and government connections. At the very least, they can afford to hire private investigators to tug at demonic Covers, but they might have connections to groups like Utopia Now, The Long Night, the Loyalists of Thule, or Network Zero, possibly even the Barret Commission or Task Force Valkyrie if Mr. Osborn makes the proper campaign donations.<br /> <br /> What purpose does Silverthorn Counseling serve, beyond &quot;blood thirsty cult&quot;? The G-M can already has destroyer angels it can deploy. Does Silverthorn Counseling maintain an Occult Matrix or Facility? Do they process and program sleepers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T21:31:10-07:00","id":1089572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1089270-advice-on-a-gm-cult?p=1089558#post1089558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much G-M backing does Silverthorn Counseling have? The Knights of St. Adrian set a precedent for an angel giving mortals, apparently on a whim, a set of endowments that let them combat demons. Perhaps different levels of initiation has a similar effect: letting adherents use effects like Voice of the Machine or City Walking. Does Arthur Osborn have an angelic minder or puppet master (An exile, perhaps)? Maybe there's a Concealment Infrastructure that prevents Demons from purchasing membership in the cult and incorporating it into an existing cover or patch job (DTD does allude that the ability of demons to make pacts is the artifact of an existing G-M system.)<br /> <br /> What mundane resources does Silverthorn Counseling have? 5,000 employees and a corporate HQ implies fluid capital, plus celebrity and government connections. At the very least, they can afford to hire private investigators to tug at demonic Covers, but they might have connections to groups like Utopia Now, The Long Night, the Loyalists of Thule, or Network Zero, possibly even the Barret Commission or Task Force Valkyrie if Mr. Osborn makes the proper campaign donations.<br /> <br /> What purpose does Silverthorn Counseling serve, beyond &quot;blood thirsty cult&quot;? The G-M can already has destroyer angels it can deploy. Does Silverthorn Counseling maintain an Occult Matrix or Facility? Do they process and program sleepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>The cult's main focus could be using their program to make unknowing Sleepers out of low level initiates who pay for the basic program. But, those that pay for the delux program get a different experience. They still do the same meditation the normal initiates do but, instead of becoming sleepers they become more and more intune with the Machine,eventually becoming Stigmatics on rank 4. The G-M probably sent one angel to help maintain the cult and place advice into Osborn's head. Osborn and his cronies have access to plenty of financial resources both in America and in Europe and Asia. I am not sure if to include a celebrity spokesperson but they do have a security force to help maintain the stability of the program.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:48:59-07:00","id":1089646,"title":"","content":"My question is, what is the focus of this cult? <br /> What type of infastructure is it tied to? What is its purpose or use? <br /> Are the cultists doing things to actually fuel or operate infastructure?<br /> Is the reason for stigmatic 'production' because that is the output of this cult and their infastructure and the stigmatics have an external use to the machine?<br /> <br /> No infastructure is truly stand alone. It is a Web of interconnected peices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}